Minimum resource requirement. We conclude this section on theoretical analysis in a fault-free sce-
nario by the following remark. We point out that all results can be extended to deal with the variant of
the problem where each task Ti has a minimum compute node requirement mi. Such a requirement is
typically provided by the user. In that variant, Equation 5.2 is defined only for j greater than mi. For
all previous algorithms, the difference lies in the preliminary step where one assigns one processor
to each task: one would now assign mi processors to task i, for all i. The number of total steps in
the algorithms becomes smaller (because there are fewer processors available). One should note that
with this constraint, all results (Theorems 5.1 through 5.6) are still valid, and proofs are quite similar.
